These artefacts were produced BEFORE two implementation bugs were found and fixed:
 (1) the NB2 log-pmf had the y and k logarithm terms swapped -> dispersion MLE was wrong
     (found by cross-check against scipy.stats.nbinom, discrepancy ~14 log units);
 (2) dispersion shrinkage let boundary estimates set tau2 to its cap -> p-values inflated.
They are kept only as a record of the debugging trail. THE DELIVERABLE RESULTS ARE IN
analysis/tables/ (de_results_WvsK_final.tsv, candidate_DE_genes_calibrated.tsv, ...).
